	<section class="fsElement fsPanelGroup fsAccordion fsPanelIconBefore" id="fsEl_16607" data-use-new="true" >

				<header>
					<h2 class="fsElementTitle" id="fsElementTitle_16607">CCSDO Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" >
		    <ul class="fsTabsNav" role="tablist">
        
            <li id="fsTab-16608" class="fsTabsNavItem " role="presentation">
                <a role='tab' aria-selected='false' href='#fs-panel-16608' aria-controls='fsEl_16608'>What is the process for proposing a transfer of territory?</a>
                
            </li>
            <li id="fsTab-16610" class="fsTabsNavItem " role="presentation">
                <a role='tab' aria-selected='false' href='#fs-panel-16610' aria-controls='fsEl_16610'>What are the requirements for a petition?</a>
                
            </li>
            <li id="fsTab-16612" class="fsTabsNavItem " role="presentation">
                <a role='tab' aria-selected='false' href='#fs-panel-16612' aria-controls='fsEl_16612'>What is the CCSDO's role in trustee area changes after the state's completion of the decennial census?</a>
                
            </li>

    </ul>

    	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsA11yPanelIconBefore fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_16608" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
					<h2 class="fsElementTitle fsA11yElementTitleIconInSpan" id="fsElementTitle_16608">
						<span aria-hidden="true"></span><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_16608' aria-expanded='false' class='accordion-trigger' id='fsAccordion_16608' href='#fs-panel-16608'>What is the process for proposing a transfer of territory?</a>
</h2>	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true" role="region" aria-labelledby="fsAccordion_16608">
		<a id="fs-panel-16608"></a>
	<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_16609" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>An action to transfer territory from one school district to another is initiated by the submission of a valid petition to the committee. To understand the various types of petitions that may be filed, please refer to the&nbsp;<a href="http://www.cde.ca.gov/re/lr/do/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">CDE District Organization Handbook</a>.&nbsp;The County Superintendent of Schools provides technical assistance to stakeholders engaged in CCSDO processes, but is impartial to decision making. The CCSDO is empowered with deliberation and action on all responsibilities that fall under its jurisdiction. &nbsp;</p>

<p>After the committee has determined a petition is valid and complete, they conduct the required public hearings, consider the information presented, &nbsp;and make a determination based on requirements specified in the Education Code to approve/ disapprove the proposal. If the committee disapproves the proposal, the process ends. If the committee approves the proposal and all affected school district governing boards have taken action to declare support for the transfer, the transfer action is implemented. If any school district governing board has taken action to oppose the transfer, an election is held in the territory selected by the committee. If the proposal passes at the election, the transfer action is implemented.&nbsp;</p>


	</div>


	</div>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsA11yPanelIconBefore fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_16610" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
					<h2 class="fsElementTitle fsA11yElementTitleIconInSpan" id="fsElementTitle_16610">
						<span aria-hidden="true"></span><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_16610' aria-expanded='false' class='accordion-trigger' id='fsAccordion_16610' href='#fs-panel-16610'>What are the requirements for a petition?</a>
</h2>	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true" role="region" aria-labelledby="fsAccordion_16610">
		<a id="fs-panel-16610"></a>
	<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_16611" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>To pursue a proposed reorganization of a school or community college district, any citizen, governing board of an LEA, and in some cases certain local agencies (e.g., county board of supervisors, city council, local agency formation commission), or county committee may present a petition for proposed reorganization.</p>

<p>The petition should include a statement of what is proposed, the names of the districts affected, a list of the reasons for such proposal, and a map and boundary description of the area involved. The Secretary will provide the format for the petition and technical assistance. The number of signatures required for a valid petition varies depending upon the type of action proposed.</p>


	</div>


	</div>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	
	<section class="fsElement fsPanel fsA11yPanelIconBefore fsStyleAutoclear" id="fsEl_16612" data-use-new="true" role="tabpanel" >

				<header>
					<h2 class="fsElementTitle fsA11yElementTitleIconInSpan" id="fsElementTitle_16612">
						<span aria-hidden="true"></span><a role='button' aria-controls='fsPanelContent_16612' aria-expanded='false' class='accordion-trigger' id='fsAccordion_16612' href='#fs-panel-16612'>What is the CCSDO's role in trustee area changes after the state's completion of the decennial census?</a>
</h2>	</header>
	<div class="fsElementContent" aria-hidden="true" role="region" aria-labelledby="fsAccordion_16612">
		<a id="fs-panel-16612"></a>
	<div class="fsElement fsContent" id="fsEl_16613" data-use-new="true" >

				<div class="fsElementContent" >
			<p>School districts which have established trustee areas in which each trustee is elected by the residents of the area they represent must rearrange the trustee area boundaries before March 1 of the year following the completion of the decennial census. &nbsp;If the local district does not adjust the boundaries within the timeframe, the CCSDO must do so before April 30 of the same year.&nbsp;</p>


	</div>


	</div>
	


	</div>


	</section>
	



	</div>


	</section>
	
